Scenario:

A teacher does not know the number of students in advance. Write a Java program using an ArrayList to store marks, display marks, find the highest mark, and calculate the average.

Program:

import java.util.ArrayList;

public class StudentMarks {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        ArrayList<Integer> marks = new ArrayList<>();

        marks.add(78);
        marks.add(85);
        marks.add(92);
        marks.add(67);
        marks.add(88);

        System.out.println("Student Marks: " + marks);

        int highest = marks.get(0);
        int sum = 0;

        for (int mark : marks) {
            if (mark > highest) {
                highest = mark;
            }
            sum += mark;
        }

        double average = (double) sum / marks.size();

        System.out.println("Highest Mark: " + highest);
        System.out.println("Average Mark: " + average);
    }
}

Output:

Student Marks: [78, 85, 92, 67, 88]
Highest Mark: 92
Average Mark: 82.0
